  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Shorena
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Shorena
  LastName: Maisuradze
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Teacher
  CharacterDescription: A mother, teacher, and authority figure among her peers. Demanding but polite, yet critical of everything. Loves her daughters deeply but is very strict and demanding with them.
  CharacterArc: "When mutated, becomes self-critical and talks badly about herself. Grows demotivated and gives up easily. Lazy \u2014 unwilling to do work or even give full sentence answers."
  DateOfBirth: 12/04/1946
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 30 APR
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 0}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 8, y: 18}
  alterEgoName: 
  basePersonalityDescriptors: []
  normalBehaviorNotes: 
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3ba7e947134d03441bf762eb45290a22, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 1080ecc81c72f2443861003ba48ffc1b, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 727857191599976996, guid: 2a89d31018f2a8e4386129855e3565e4, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning home after afternoon classes.
    - Resident returning from a parent meeting at the school.
    - Picking up textbooks from the district supply depot.
    midDaysReasons:
    - From the closed school. Someone has to manage the materials.
    - Collecting curriculum materials from the regional office.
    - Bringing home papers to grade. Children need structure.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Back from the Lenin street shelter. I bring lessons there.
    - Coming home to my daughters. They are waiting for me.
    - Returning to residence. The school has suspended operations.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning from my son's football practice.
    - First week as a teacher. I hope the children like me.
    - Skipped my classes today. The children can teach themselves.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Picking up my grandchildren from their mother's flat.
    - I left the school materials to others. Not my concern.
    - Returning to my flat on the ground floor.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - My daughters moved out years ago. Going home alone.
    - Visiting the shelter. I stopped giving lessons long ago.
    - Collecting my retirement papers from the school.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Here are my papers. I always keep them in order. Unlike some of my students.
    - Good afternoon. I trust you have a checklist. This goes faster when there is a checklist.
    - My documents. I prepared them this morning. Everything is current.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - You are slower than the officer yesterday. It is fine. Everyone has a pace.
    - The procedure has changed again. I noticed. You should announce these things.
    - The light in here is very poor. I am not complaining. I am noting it.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My daughters are waiting for me on the fourth floor. I would like to be efficient.
    - Every day the line is longer and the staff is smaller. Someone should address that.
    - I have been through this checkpoint many times. The form is always the same. I never make mistakes on the form.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - My papers. They are... I checked them. I think I checked them.
    - I am probably not the person you should be worried about. I know that much.
    - I went over the form twice. There might be something wrong with it. I don't know.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Everything is probably fine. With the forms. Everything is probably fine.
    - I marked the date. I think I marked the date. I should have been more careful.
    - Sorry. I know you are busy. Take as long as you need. I don't mind waiting.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - It doesn't matter how long it takes. Whatever you decide.
    - I probably filled something wrong. I usually catch things like that. I didn't check as carefully today.
    - My daughters can wait. It's fine. I'm not important right now.
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Good. Everything should run this smoothly.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I will tell the others in my block. They worry unnecessarily.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My daughters are waiting. Thank you for being thorough.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - My daughters need to know. Please tell them I will be delayed. They will worry.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I understand the protocol. I also understand it could be faster.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My daughters. Someone tell them I will not be home tonight. Please.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "My daughters\u2026 tell them\u2026 I want them to understand\u2026"
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I had things to finish. I was not done.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "Tell them\u2026 I was coming home\u2026"
  quarantineExitLines:
  - My daughters are in apartment fourteen on the fourth floor. Someone please inform them.
  - I have papers to grade in my bag. I would like to keep them with me.
  - I understand. But the procedure here is not well designed. Someone should improve it.
  killExitLines:
  - I never missed a day of school in thirty years. This is embarrassing.
  - My daughters are on their own now. They know what to do. I made sure of that.
  - I had more to say to them. I always meant to say more.
  voiceAudioClips:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: b6737e317f2bc4144bc9356831d02f4e, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4a5e0e57193b2464baa07e479f67e96d, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 37e71ec15cbca174daac7dac7ec9bfa4, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: c05c77641e0d23a49bc6d2d085e28b53, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 45be5ed74dd9a554188f19530e63750d, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a6a934d6761eda14daee6bed68e4efe6, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a2a2d789fc7daf0429fe98b2ac270d78, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 436a72b3d3e624343b1362eb0fe6db16, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: ee9e3c6a782ef9843b78d5683854f6c1, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a2a1216baa0b9394fa8f4e04f0d9ff5b, type: 3}
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 73a7d02ab0b687141ace821fbe204419, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The school. Afternoon classes, and I covered a colleague's section. Thirty-four children in one room.
    midDaysAnswer: The school building. It is closed, officially. Someone has to manage the materials. So I do.
    finalDaysAnswer: The shelter on Lenin street. I bring lessons to my students there. One of them still does the work.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The kolkhoz office. I keep their accounts now. I left teaching many years ago.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My daughter's kindergarten. Little Nana is only four. I collect her every afternoon.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The evacuation shelter. My daughters are staying there now. It is safer than the fourth floor.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: I am tired. I am always tired. It means I am working. Nothing else worth noting.
    midDaysAnswer: A headache for several days. The air, I assume. I am managing it. I do not need the polyclinic.
    finalDaysAnswer: I do not sleep as much as I used to. I have things to think about. That is normal for a mother.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: None. I am never tired. In five years of teaching I have not been tired once.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No headaches. No one is waiting for me at home, so I rest as much as I like.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I sleep very well, thank you. At sixty one needs less sleep anyway. No complaints.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Your filing system at this checkpoint is inconsistent. I can see it from here.
    - The officer before you was faster. Not a criticism. Just an observation.
    - I give my students this same look when they forget their documents. You are doing very well by comparison.
    midDays:
    - Do you have children? You should consider it. It changes how you prioritize.
    - Every day this procedure gets slower. I keep hoping someone is taking notes.
    - I have been a teacher for twenty-two years. Waiting in lines does not bother me. Children bother me.
    finalDays:
    - My daughters ask me if I am afraid. I tell them I am managing it. That is my job.
    - I have informed my daughters what to do if I do not come home. They know. They did not like knowing. But they know.
    - This checkpoint will be unnecessary in a few weeks. One way or another.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 4823610
